es Overview Part-Time Faculty for the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner DNP Program. Responsibilities Teach psychiatric mental health nurse practitioner courses, perform outcomes assessment at the course level and other levels as requested by the Nursing department head, and maintain attendance records. Minimum Qualifications Applicant must have a Master’s Degree in Nursing with an earned doctorate in Nursing or related field (or near completion) and certification as a PMHNP.  Must possess current Pennsylvania license or eligibility for RN licensure in Pennsylvania. Past teaching experience preferred. Act 153 Clearance Required Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check No Required to Pass a Credit Check No Additional Posting Information None Special Applicant Instructions None Advertised: July 15, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App SEARCH RESULTS POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Part-Time Faculty-DNP Psych Mental Health DNP Nursing Program Moon Campus Part-Time Faculty for the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner DNP Program. POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Part-Time Faculty-DNP Psych Mental Health DNP Nursing Program Moon Campus Part-Time Faculty for the Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner DNP Program. Powered by PageUp Contact | Campus Map Main navigation Why Choose RMU? WHY CHOOSE RMU? Reputation and Outcomes RMU is Affordable Campus Experience Thriving City Personal Attention Flexible Learning Athletic Tradition Admissions ADMISSIONS Freshman Admissions Graduate & Doctoral Admissions Transfer Admissions International Admissions Part-time, Readmission and Guest Students Veterans & Military Families Student Financial Services Financial Aid Office College Affordability Academy Academics ACADEMICS Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Doctoral Programs Certificate Programs Online Programs Schools & Departments Office of the Provost Special Academic Programs R