ition will make visits to students in the clinical setting in collaboration with the lead course faculty member. Responsibilities: Responsibilities include visiting the assigned students at the clinical site; interacting and problem solving with the preceptor; communicating with the lead course faculty member and the students; supervising and grading of student paperwork including Subjective, Objective, Assessment and Plan (SOAP) note. Minimum Qualifications: Must be a licensed Nurse Practitioner; Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) is preferred but not required. Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check: No Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: July 15, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App SEARCH RESULTS POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Part-Time Faculty-DNP Site Adviser DNP Nursing Program Moon Campus Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) Site Adviser position will make visits to students in the clinical setting in collaboration with the lead course faculty member. POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Part-Time Faculty-DNP Site Adviser DNP Nursing Program Moon Campus Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) Site Adviser position will make visits to students in the clinical s