rses in the Family Nurse Practitioner DNP Program. Responsibilities: Teach Family Nurse Practitioner courses, perform outcomes assessment at the course level and other levels as requested by the Nursing Department Head, and maintain attendance records. Minimum Qualifications: Applicant must have a Master’s Degree in Nursing with an earned Doctorate in Nursing or related field (or near completion) and certification as an FNP. Must possess current Pennsylvania license or eligibility for RN licensure in Pennsylvania. Past teaching experience preferred. Act 153 Clearance Required: Yes Required To Pass a Motor Vehicle Report Check (If driving on behalf of the University): No Required to Pass a Credit Check: No Additional Posting Information: None Special Applicant Instructions: None Commitment to Diversity: Robert Morris University is committed to increasing diversity in our community and actively pursues individuals from all backgrounds. Additionally, RMU complies with all applicable federal, state and local laws and provides equal opportunity in all educational programs and activities, admission of students and conditions of employment for all qualified individuals regardless of race, color, sex, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation, or national origin. Reasonable Accommodation Notice: Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please email humanresources@rmu.edu or call us at (412) 397-6270 if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job or to perform your job. Advertised: July 13, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App SEARCH RESULTS POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Part-Time Faculty-DNP, Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) Program DNP Nursing Program Moon Campus Part-Time Faculty to teach courses in the Family Nurse Practitioner DNP Program. POSITION DEPARTMENT LOCATION Part-Time Faculty-DNP, Family Nurse Practit